# Changes to these paths need a review from the repository owner. They hold
# the security-sensitive parts of vogel: authentication, authorization, the
# HTTP edge, input decoding, the audit trail, database and storage access,
# the workflow engine, migrations, CI and the security policy. With branch
# protection set to "Require review from Code Owners", a PR touching them
# cannot merge without that review.
#
# Later rules win over earlier ones; keep the specific paths below.

/auth/       @Kafeiih
/authz/      @Kafeiih
/access/     @Kafeiih
/httpx/      @Kafeiih
/request/    @Kafeiih
/audit/      @Kafeiih
/postgres/   @Kafeiih
/storage/    @Kafeiih
/workflow/   @Kafeiih
/migrate/    @Kafeiih
/.github/    @Kafeiih
/SECURITY.md @Kafeiih

# Module files: a dependency change is a supply-chain change, in the library
# and in the boilerplate consumers copy.
/go.mod                      @Kafeiih
/go.sum                      @Kafeiih
/examples/boilerplate/go.mod @Kafeiih
/examples/boilerplate/go.sum @Kafeiih

# The boilerplate's authorization policies decide who may do what in every
# service generated from it.
/examples/boilerplate/cerbos/ @Kafeiih

# The release workflow template: it decides what a generated service
# publishes and with which permissions.
/examples/boilerplate/.github/ @Kafeiih
